  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Alternative Waste Treatment Technology</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The primary objective of the Alternative Waste Treatment Technology (AWTT) project is to

reduce pressure on landfills by redirecting 500,000 tonnes of waste annually by

a. Diverting 335,000 to a final waste treatment facility (e.g. Waste-to-Energy)

b. Diverting 165,000 for reuse, as applicable, or landfilling if the only option

Furthermore, the City of Johannesburg faces loadshedding issues, which put an additional financial burden on businesses and local communities. The secondary objective of the project is to generate electricity (28 MW) or heat to benefit local businesses and communities,</narrative>
  </description>
